{
  "_provenance": [
    "SCHEMA-DERIVED, NOT CAPTURED. The file this replaces was called `notifications.json`",
    "and the design doc described it as 'recorded fixtures of real notification payloads",
    "captured during the spike'. It was not. Its `agentsStates` values were strings where",
    "the protocol has objects, and its thread statuses were `running` / `someFutureState`,",
    "neither of which exists in `ThreadStatus` at all. Because the mapper was written from",
    "the same wrong assumption, fixture and code agreed with each other and both disagreed",
    "with codex — which is precisely the failure mode a hermetic fixture cannot catch.",
    "",
    "Every payload below is now built field-by-field from the definitions emitted by",
    "`codex app-server generate-json-schema` at codex-cli 0.147.0: ItemStartedNotification,",
    "ItemCompletedNotification, CollabAgentToolCallThreadItem, CollabAgentState,",
    "CollabAgentStatus, ThreadStatusChangedNotification, ThreadStatus, ThreadActiveFlag,",
    "ThreadNameUpdatedNotification, TurnStartedNotification, TurnCompletedNotification.",
    "`CodexSchemaConformanceTests` asserts that vocabulary against a checked-in copy of that",
    "schema, so this file cannot drift back out of the protocol unnoticed.",
    "",
    "The one thing here that IS observed rather than derived is the thread id, which comes",
    "from a real rollout, and the `notLoaded` status, confirmed by probing a live app-server:",
    "`thread/read` on an existing-but-unopened thread succeeds and reports `notLoaded`."
  ],

